#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2141
msgid ""
"Providers you trust (a local Ollama, say) follow their own column of values, "
"\"What trusted providers may use\", Allow for everything unless you change "
"it, so nothing is asked for requests that go to them. A book's own Never "
"still wins.\n"
"\n"
"A standing Allow is also what background features (Automatic X-Ray, "
"checkpoint builds) need: with a trusted provider they build without a "
"question."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2148
msgid "What trusted providers may use"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2149
msgid ""
"The value of each kind of data for requests that go to a trusted provider. "
"Allow by default: nothing is asked. Ask or Never here applies to trusted "
"providers only; every other provider follows the rows below."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2160
msgid ""
"Your reading progress, the current chapter and the time since you last read. "
"Sent or not; never asked."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2177
msgid "Preset: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2180
msgid ""
"One tap sets every kind of data below for all books. Default (Ask) puts "
"every value back to the one it ships with: Ask, with reading position and "
"the text around what you tap sent, and Allow for trusted providers. Allow "
"everything sends every kind without a question, book text included (it "
"raises token costs). Block everything sets every kind to Never: only your "
"question, the selected text and the book info go (and the behavior, domain "
"and Background texts, which no preset touches); reading position goes off "
"too, so spoiler protection no longer knows where you are. Allow everything "
"and Block everything leave the trusted providers' own values alone, and "
"every preset keeps the books' own values and Book info. The row names the "
"preset your values match, or Custom."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2189
msgid "Tip: Per-book values"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2190
msgid ""
"Every kind of data here can have its own value for one book (Book Settings → "
"Privacy & Data, or \"Allow for this book\" in the question). A book's Never "
"always wins, even over trusted providers; its Allow sends without asking."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2202
msgid ""
"Your personal notes attached to highlights. Allowing notes allows highlights "
"too. Used by Analyze Notes, Connect with Notes, and actions with "
"{annotations} placeholders."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2222
msgid ""
"Your highlighted passages, without the notes. Never here is Never for notes "
"too. Used by Recap, Analyze Notes, and actions with {highlights} "
"placeholders. X-Ray does not send them: it only matches them locally, to "
"offer them on an entity page."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2236
msgid ""
"Your notebook for the book. Used by Connect with Notes, \"Chat about this "
"notebook\", the Attach chip and actions with the {notebook} placeholder."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2244
msgid ""
"Your reading progress (percentage), the current chapter, chapters read and "
"the time since you last read. On by default: spoiler protection relies on "
"it. Sent or not; never asked. Used by X-Ray, Recap."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2253
msgid ""
"The titles, authors and reading status of the books in your scan folders, "
"for the library actions. Configure permanent scan folders in Reading & "
"Library, or pick folders on the fly in the input dialog. The question offers "
"\"Always allow\", which sets Allow here."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2262
msgid ""
"Groups made from your reading statistics (books read extensively, stalled "
"reads, briefly started), computed on the device; only the lists leave it. "
"Used by the library actions."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2271
msgid ""
"The bounded text around a selection (the context of a highlight or a "
"dictionary lookup), your current page (page translate, the Scope chip's "
"\"Current page\") and the text around an image prompt: a few sentences or "
"one page, never more. Allow by default; independent of book text, so a book "
"can keep its text to itself while these still work."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2287
msgid ""
"What the AI is told about the book with every request: the title, the "
"author, and with \"Title, author & position\" your reading progress, chapter "
"and page (when Reading position is on). Never asked, and the presets leave "
"it alone. None sends nothing that names the book: no book line, and an "
"action's own prompt says \"this book\" where it would name the title; "
"actions that answer from what the AI knows about the book (About, Find "
"Similar, Reviews…) cannot run then, and say so. Image prompts follow it too. "
"Override per book in Book Settings → Privacy & Data; one chat can switch it "
"with the gear menu's Send book info, one run with the hold menu's Without "
"book info."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2297
msgid "Text Extraction (book text: %1)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2308
msgid ""
"The book's own text, up to your position or the whole of it: X-Ray, Recap, "
"Summarize, book tools and actions with text placeholders. Ask (the default): "
"the first action that wants it asks, and \"Allow for this book\" keeps your "
"answer. Allow: sent without a question, and background features (Automatic X-"
"Ray, checkpoint builds) run on it. Never: those actions are refused.\n"
"\n"
"Text raises token costs. Tip: Use Hidden Flows to exclude front matter, "
"appendices, etc. You can also focus actions on a specific section or section "
"range to extract only a chapter or part; for X-Ray, checkpoints cover the "
"book in bounded incremental steps."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2314
msgid ""
"Book text goes to the AI without a question now, for every book without its "
"own value. This uses tokens (increases API costs) and processing time; "
"background features you opt into separately (such as Automatic X-Ray) will "
"also read text without asking.\n"
"\n"
"Tip: Use Hidden Flows to exclude front matter, appendices, etc. You can also "
"focus actions on a specific section or section range to extract only a "
"chapter or part; for X-Ray, checkpoints cover the book in bounded "
"incremental steps."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2322
msgid "Max Text Characters"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2329
msgid ""
"Maximum characters to extract (100,000-10,000,000). Higher = more context "
"but more tokens. Default: 4,000,000 (~1M tokens). The API will reject "
"requests that exceed the model's context window.\n"
"\n"
"Tip: Use Hidden Flows to exclude irrelevant content, or focus on a specific "
"section instead of the full document."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2338
msgid "Max Pages (PDF, DJVU, CBZ…)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2345
msgid ""
"Maximum pages to extract from page-based formats like PDF, DJVU, and CBZ "
"(100-5,000). Higher = more context but slower. Default: 2,000.\n"
"\n"
"Tip: Use Hidden Flows to exclude irrelevant pages, or focus on a specific "
"section instead of the full document."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2354
msgid "Don't warn about truncated extractions"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2357
msgid ""
"When unchecked, a blocking warning is shown before sending requests when "
"extracted text was truncated to fit the character limit. Shows coverage "
"percentage so you know how much of the book was included.\n"
"\n"
"Background runs (Automatic X-Ray, checkpoint builds) never show this "
"warning: a truncated background extraction aborts the run instead of sending "
"dishonest coverage.\n"
"\n"
"Check this if you don't need the reminder."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2366
msgid "Don't warn about large extractions"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2369
msgid ""
"When unchecked, a warning is shown before sending requests with large text "
"extractions (over 500K characters / ~125K tokens). Most models have smaller "
"context windows and will reject oversized requests.\n"
"\n"
"Background runs (Automatic X-Ray, checkpoint builds) never show this "
"warning; their size is bounded instead: automatic updates by the Maximum "
"Progress Gap, checkpoints by their incremental steps.\n"
"\n"
"Check this if you know your model's limits and don't need the reminder."
msgstr ""

