msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2858
msgid ""
"Delete all chat history?\n"
"\n"
"This removes all saved conversations across all books.\n"
"\n"
"This cannot be undone."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2870
msgid "Advanced"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2888
msgid "Maximum"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2889
msgid "Global stance: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2891
msgid ""
"How much reasoning across all models, as far as each model allows. Override "
"individual models below."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2905
msgid "Per-model reasoning"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2913
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3031
msgid "Show Indicator in Chat"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2914
msgid ""
"Include reasoning in the combined usage indicator line (e.g. '*[Reasoning/"
"Thinking was used]*') when reasoning is requested or used.\n"
"\n"
"Full reasoning content is always viewable via 'Show Reasoning' button."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2934
msgid ""
"Range: 0.0-2.0 (Anthropic max 1.0)\n"
"Lower = focused, deterministic\n"
"Higher = creative, varied\n"
"\n"
"Applies to free-form chat: most built-in actions set their own temperature."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2942
msgid "ignored by this model"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2943
msgid "fixed by this model"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2950
msgid ""
"Applies to free-form chat: most built-in actions set their own temperature.\n"
"Some models ignore this setting or accept only a fixed value; the row says "
"so when the current model is one of them."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2962
msgid "Faster Models for Quick Actions"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2965
msgid ""
"Actions that declare a speed tier (Translate, Quick Define and Quick Explain "
"by default; configurable per action in the action editor) use a faster model "
"from your current provider for that request. Only the model changes; the "
"prompt and settings stay the same. Providers without tier data keep the "
"current model. Turn off to always use your configured model."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2974
msgid "Tier Models (Global)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2986
msgid "Supported: %1 (other providers currently ignore this)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2992
msgid "Enable Web Search"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:2993
msgid ""
"Allow AI to search the web for current information.\n"
"\n"
"Supported providers: %1.\n"
"\n"
"Gemini supports it only on Search-grounding-capable models; OpenAI on GPT-5 "
"models and xAI on Grok-4 models (via their Responses APIs); OpenRouter works "
"for any model via the :online suffix.\n"
"\n"
"Perplexity searches BY DEFAULT (its native behavior); the Web toggle can now "
"actually turn it off per chat or per book.\n"
"\n"
"Other providers currently ignore this setting.\n"
"\n"
"This is a global default: per-request toggles (input dialog, chat viewer) "
"adapt to the active provider.\n"
"\n"
"Increases token usage/cost."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3000
msgid ""
"Note: on Gemini, web search means Google Search grounding, which is billed "
"against its own quota -- separate from normal requests, and on the free tier "
"sometimes zero. If searching actions fail with a quota error while plain "
"ones work, that is the usual cause."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3015
msgid "Web Search Effort: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3017
msgid ""
"How much web searching the AI may do per question.\n"
"\n"
"Light: fewest searches, fastest and cheapest.\n"
"Standard: balanced (provider defaults).\n"
"Thorough: most searches and context, slower and costlier.\n"
"\n"
"Applies where the provider offers control: Anthropic (up to 2/5/10 "
"searches), OpenAI and Perplexity (search context size), OpenRouter (3/5/10 "
"results), Z.AI (result count and snippet size). Gemini and xAI decide "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3032
msgid ""
"Include web search in the combined usage indicator line (e.g. '*[Web search "
"was used]*') when web search is used.\n"
"\n"
"Streaming indicator ('Searching the web...') is always shown."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3042
msgid "Image Generation"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3046
msgid "Generate images from highlighted text (button in the highlight menu)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3055
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3067
msgid "Follow main provider"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3063
msgid ""
"Which provider generates images.\n"
"\n"
"'Follow main provider' uses your current chat provider when it supports "
"images (OpenAI, xAI, Gemini, OpenRouter). Picking one explicitly lets image "
"generation work no matter which chat provider is active: it uses that "
"provider's own API key.\n"
"\n"
"The highlight-menu button appears when the provider in effect has an API "
"key. If your chat provider can't make images, it appears when any image "
"provider has a key, and the first tap asks which one to use (the answer is "
"saved here)."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3080
msgid "OpenAI model: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3082
msgid ""
"gpt-image-2.5-flare is fast (about 11 s at low quality) and cheap; gpt-"
"image-2.5-sunburst gives the finest detail but is slower."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3093
msgid "xAI model: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3095
msgid ""
"grok-imagine-image is fast and the cheapest; grok-imagine-image-2.0 makes "
"better pictures at about twice the price."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3106
msgid "Gemini model: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3108
msgid ""
"Nano Banana 2.1 is Google's everyday image model; Flash Lite is the fastest "
"and cheapest; 3 Pro gives the finest detail but is slower."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3123
msgid "OpenRouter model: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3125
msgid ""
"OpenRouter draws with many makers' models through one key. GPT Image 2.5 "
"Flare is fast and the cheapest (about half a cent at Draft); Nano Banana 2.1 "
"is Google's everyday model; FLUX 3 (Black Forest Labs, about 5 cents), its "
"small model FLUX 3 Klein (about a cent, and quick) and Seedream 5.0 Flash "
"(ByteDance, about 2 cents) are other makers'; Recraft v4.1 Flash (under a "
"cent) leans to illustration.\n"
"\n"
"More models… lists OpenRouter's whole image catalog. Shape and Detail adapt "
"to what the picked model takes."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3134
msgid "Shape: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3136
msgid ""
"The picture's proportions, for every image provider.\n"
"\n"
"Fit my screen matches your screen as you hold it, so the picture fills an e-"
"reader's page. Portrait, Landscape and Square are fixed. Let the model "
"choose leaves it to the provider, which often draws a square or a wide "
"picture.\n"
"\n"
"Each model gets the nearest proportions it can draw; OpenAI's 2.5 models "
"draw your screen's own."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3146
msgid "Detail: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3148
msgid ""
"How much detail a picture gets, for every image provider. Draft is the "
"fastest and cheapest; Best is the slowest and costs the most.\n"
"\n"
"OpenAI: quality low, medium or high (xhigh on the 2.5 models). xAI: grok-"
"imagine-image-2.0 draws at low or medium quality, and Best at 2k. Gemini: "
"Best draws at 2K, Draft and Standard at 1K, and at Draft Nano Banana 2.1 and "
"Pro think as little as they can before drawing, which makes a picture "
"faster.\n"
"\n"
"Grayed out while the model in use has a single setting (grok-imagine-image, "
"Gemini Flash Lite)."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3160
msgid "Write the prompt with AI"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3163
msgid ""
"Before each picture, your chat provider's fast model writes the prompt the "
"image model receives: from the passage, the text around it, the book's title "
"and author, the book's Background, the X-Ray entries the passage names and "
"your note, under rules that keep it to what the book says (and, with spoiler "
"protection on, to nothing later than the passage).\n"
"\n"
"It adds one quick text request (a fraction of a cent) and sends that "
"material to your chat provider (or to the provider a global Fast tier pin "
"names) as well. The viewer's caption and the gallery say who wrote the "
"prompt and from what.\n"
"\n"
"Off: the passage goes to the image model framed as before."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3173
msgid "Style: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3175
msgid ""
"How pictures look, for every image provider: Book illustration (the "
"default), Watercolor, Ink drawing, Pencil sketch, Woodcut, Photographic, "
"Comic, Map or diagram, or Custom… (your own words, such as \"a 1920s travel "
"poster\").\n"
"\n"
"The prompt writer works it into the prompt; with the writer off it is one "
"line at the end of the prompt."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3185
msgid "Include book title/author in prompt"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3188
msgid ""
"Frame image prompts with the book's title and author, so illustrations can "
"match the work's setting and era.\n"
"\n"
"Applies when generating from a book."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3193
msgid "Include surrounding text in prompt"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3196
msgid ""
"Add a short slice of the text around the selection, marked as context only, "
"so the illustration reflects the scene the passage sits in."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3201
msgid "Prompt template…"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3204
msgid ""
"Shows what goes to the models, with your current settings applied: the "
"prompt writer's instructions and the material it reads when Write the prompt "
"with AI is on, and the framed prompt (the writer's fallback, or the prompt "
"itself with the writer off)."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3210
msgid "Generated images…"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3213
msgid ""
"The images generated so far, as thumbnails, by book: tap one to view it; "
"hold it to read its prompt, draw that prompt again (as it stands or edited, "
"in the Style now in effect, beside the old picture or in its place), change "
"the image settings on the spot, or delete it."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3221
msgid "Provider Settings"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3235
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3300
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3322
msgid "International"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3236
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3301
#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3323
msgid "China"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3238
msgid "Z.AI Region: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3240
msgid ""
"Select the Z.AI API endpoint.\n"
"\n"
"The same API key works on both endpoints:\n"
"- International: api.z.ai\n"
"- China: open.bigmodel.cn"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3255
msgid "Jina (international)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3262
msgid "Z.AI Search Engine: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3264
msgid ""
"Search engine used for Z.AI web search.\n"
"\n"
"The international engines (Jina, Bing) return much better sources for non-"
"Chinese queries. The Chinese-web engines suit Chinese-language content."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3282
msgid "Gemini Content Filter: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3283
msgid "Relaxed for books"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3285
msgid ""
"Google's default content filter can block answers about violent or sexual "
"passages in books. The reply then arrives empty, with the reason named.\n"
"\n"
"Relaxed turns the four adjustable filter categories off for this plugin's "
"requests. Google default sends no filter setting."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3302
msgid "US"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3304
msgid "Qwen Region: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3306
msgid ""
"Select your Alibaba Cloud region.\n"
"\n"
"API keys are region-specific and NOT interchangeable:\n"
"- International: Singapore (dashscope-intl)\n"
"- China: Beijing (dashscope)\n"
"- US: Virginia (dashscope-us)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3325
msgid "Kimi Region: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3327
msgid ""
"Select the Kimi (Moonshot) platform your API key was issued on.\n"
"\n"
"Keys are NOT interchangeable between the two platforms:\n"
"- International: platform.kimi.ai (api.moonshot.ai)\n"
"- China: platform.moonshot.cn (api.moonshot.cn)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3343
msgid ""
"EXPERIMENTAL: for providers and models that support tool calls (Test "
"provider shows whether yours does). Book tools let the AI search the open "
"book's text, read specific pages, and view the table of contents, so it can "
"ground answers in the actual book instead of guessing. Requires the book's "
"text to be allowed (a book on Ask is asked first).\n"
"\n"
"This sets whether the Tools chip in book chats starts ON or OFF; you can "
"always flip it per chat, and the AI still decides per question whether to "
"actually search.\n"
"\n"
"Predefined actions are unaffected either way; they never use tools unless "
"they explicitly offer smart retrieval. Override per book in Book Settings. "
"Work in progress; behavior may change."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3354
msgid "Gather then answer"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3355
msgid "Interactive"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3357
msgid "Book Tools Mode: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3359
msgid ""
"How AI Book Tools answer.\n"
"\n"
"Gather then answer: the AI quietly collects passages from the book first, "
"then answers as a normal request: the answer streams and web search stays "
"available.\n"
"\n"
"Interactive: the original agentic loop; the AI narrates its way through "
"lookups; no streaming or web search while tools run."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3363
msgid "Gather then answer (streams; recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3364
msgid "Interactive agentic loop"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3378
msgid "Book Tools Lookup Effort: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3380
msgid ""
"How much searching AI Book Tools may do per question.\n"
"\n"
"Quick: up to 4 lookups in 2 rounds, fastest, for simple factual questions.\n"
"Standard: up to 8 lookups in 4 rounds, a good balance.\n"
"Thorough: up to 16 lookups in 6 rounds, with a larger passage budget; slower "
"and costlier, for questions that need evidence from many places in the book."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3392
msgid "AI Book Tools: Read Short Texts Whole"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3393
msgid ""
"When the readable text (up to your position while spoiler protection is on) "
"is no longer than this, the AI gets it in one piece instead of searching it. "
"Small: about 16,000 characters (some 4,000 tokens). Medium: 64,000, the "
"default. Large: 128,000. Non-Latin scripts count two to three bytes per "
"character. The text goes with every message of a chat, placed so that "
"providers which cache prompts charge the repeats at a fraction; when the "
"model's known limits cannot take it, the book is searched instead. Off: "
"always search, whatever the length."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3408
msgid "AI Book Tools: Show Indicator in Chat"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3409
msgid ""
"Include book lookups in the combined usage indicator line (e.g. '*[Book "
"search (3 lookups) was used]*') when AI Book Tools ran for a response.\n"
"\n"
"The individual lookups are always viewable via the chat menu's 'Show "
"Sources' entry."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3416
msgid "AI Book Tools: Show Lookups (debug)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3419
msgid ""
"Append the tool lookups, raw tool results, and token usage to each answer "
"when AI Book Tools run. For debugging the experimental tools: leave off for "
"clean answers. Note: the raw tool results can include book-text snippets."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3425
msgid "Console Debug"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3426
msgid ""
"Log requests, responses, routing decisions and feature diagnostics to the "
"console/crash log, for developers. Large content is truncated (see below); "
"API keys are never logged. Slows page turns slightly while X-Ray marking is "
"on."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3448
msgid "Show Debug in Chat"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3449
msgid "Display debug information in chat viewer"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3459
msgid "Names"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3459
msgid "Full"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3460
msgid "Debug Detail Level: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3467
msgid "Minimal (messages only)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3468
msgid "Names (config summary)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3469
msgid "Full (system blocks)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3475
msgid "Truncate Large Content (debug)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant/ui/settings_schema.lua:3476
msgid ""
